<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">ʻIolani Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882</span> · Also known as Iolani Palace</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">ʻIolani Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a> was the royal residence of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, completed in 1882 for King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalakaua">Kalākaua</a> and lit by electricity from 1887. After the overthrow of the monarchy in 1893 it served as the seat of the provisional government, the Republic of Hawaii and later the territorial government. Queen Liliʻuokalani was imprisoned in one of its rooms in 1895 after a failed royalist rising.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iolani-palace.jpg" alt="ʻIolani Palace" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gage Skidmore from Surprise, AZ, United States of America · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iolani_Palace_(51872681413).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
